gaussian_filtered_image = imgaussfilt(double(gray_image), 3); % Standard deviation of 3 pixels
% Define Sobel operators in x and y directions
sobel_x = [-1 0 1; -2 0 2; -1 0 1];
sobel_y = [-1 -2 -1; 0 0 0; 1 2 1];
% Apply Sobel operator in x direction to gaussian filtered image
edge_image_x = conv2(double(gaussian_filtered_image), sobel_x, 'same');
% Apply Sobel operator in y direction to gaussian filtered image
edge_image_y = conv2(double(gaussian_filtered_image), sobel_y, 'same');
% Combine edges in both directions
edge_image = sqrt(edge_image_x.^2 + edge_image_y.^2);
% Display edge image
imshow(edge_image);
```
This code reads the input image, converts it to grayscale, applies a Gaussian filter with a standard deviation of 3 pixels to reduce the noise, and then applies the Sobel operator in both x and y directions to find the edges. The resulting edges are displayed using the `imshow` function.

