 To convert a given phrase to its Morse Code representation using MATLAB, you can follow these steps:
1. Define a lookup table that maps each character to its corresponding Morse Code representation.
2. Convert the input phrase to uppercase using the `upper` function.
3. Iterate through each character in the input phrase and look up its Morse Code representation in the lookup table using the `char2index` and `lookup` functions.
4. Concatenate the Morse Code representations of all characters to form the output string.
Here's the MATLAB code to do this:
```matlab
% Define Morse Code lookup table
morseCode = struct('Char', cellstr(string(65:90)'), 'MorseCode', {'".-", "-...", "--.", "..", "..-.", "--", "....", "..", ".---", "-.-", ".-..", "--.", "-----", ".----", "..---", "...--", "....-", ".....", "-....", "--...", "---..", "----."});
% Input phrase
inputPhrase = 'HELLO WORLD';
% Convert input phrase to uppercase
inputPhraseUpper = upper(inputPhrase);
% Initialize empty vector to store Morse Code representations
morseOutput = [];
% Iterate through each character in the input phrase and append its Morse Code representation to the output vector
for i = 1:length(inputPhraseUpper)
    % Look up Morse Code representation of current character
    morseRepresentation = lookup(morseCode, char2index(inputPhraseUpper(i)));
    % Append Morse Code representation to output vector
    morseOutput = [morseOutput; morseRepresentation.MorseCode];
end
% Display Morse Code representation of input phrase
disp(strjoin(morseOutput, ' '));
```
