Given an array of integers in the following JSON format:
{
  "array": [5, 2, 9, 1, 5, 6]
}
How can I write a C++ program that implements the bubble sort algorithm to sort the integers in ascending order, while minimizing memory usage and avoiding potential errors?
Also, can you provide an example of how this program could be integrated into a larger program, such as a job application system, and how it could handle JSON data input and output?

response:
 To write a C++ program for bubble sort algorithm using minimal memory and avoiding potential errors, follow the steps below:

1. Define a function to perform bubble sort:
```cpp
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;
void bubbleSort(int arr[], int n) {
    for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {
        for (int j = 0; j < n - i - 1; j++) {
            if (arr[j] > arr[j+1]) {
                swap(arr[j], arr[j+1]);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

2. Create a main function to read JSON data, call bubbleSort(), and display sorted data:
```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <nlohmann/json.hpp> // Install json library: https://github.com/nlohmann/json
using json = nlohmann::json;
int main() {
    std::string jsonString = R"({"array":[5,2,9,1,5,6]})"; // Replace with JSON string from your source
    json j = json::parse(jsonString);

    int size = j["array"].size();
    std::vector<int> arr(j["array"].begin(), j["array"].end());

    bubbleSort(arr.data(), size);

    cout << "[";
    for (int i = 0; i < size-1; i++) {
        cout << arr[i] << ", ";
    }
    cout << arr[size-1] << "]\n";

    return 0;
}
```

